# TEST_MODE : MULTI_MODULE_OK

# PRIVATE NAKED procedures across SEPARATELY COMPILED modules.
#
# -gen gcc emitted every naked procedure as a '.globl' asm label with only a
# C prototype, 'static' for a private one -- so gcc warned "'F' used but
# never defined", and two modules including the same header with a private
# naked procedure failed to link:
#
#     multiple definition of `NAKEDINC'
#
# Dropping the '.globl' alone is not enough on PE/COFF: gcc marks every
# extern function a module references '.scl 2' (external), and an undefined
# 'static' one becomes extern after the warning.  A private (or weak) naked
# procedure is now a real 'static' C function with __attribute__((naked)), so
# it is module-private, as it already was with -gen gas64.  A public one stays
# a '.globl' label (NakedPublicDouble, defined in module A and called from the
# driver).  A single-module test cannot see this, which is why this is a .bmk.
#
# Reported by xSmartPtr as b03.

MAIN := naked-private-mm-main.bas
SRCS := naked-private-mm-a.bas
